WEBVTT

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:29.960
Welcome to Mutual of Omaha's Wild Kingdom, the Great Sea of Sawgrass.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.820
making up the Florida Everglades, here in the southern portion of that state,

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:39.410
is one of the wildest primitive marsh areas remaining in this country.

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:45.190
Throughout this expansive area of shallow, slow-moving water and sawgrass,

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:49.080
there are numerous small islands called hammocks.

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:53.000
They are very low with stunted and gnarled tree growth,

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:57.740
but they're the only areas of dry ground in the thousands of square miles

00:00:57.740 --> 00:00:59.280
which make up the Everglades.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.260
Because they are dry areas slightly higher than their surroundings, they become havens

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:07.120
for a wide variety of wildlife.

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:16.180
Here the Everglades deer and bear, panther and otter, and a multitude of other creatures

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:21.700
come to rest, feed, and raise families, and many confrontations between these animals

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:22.220
occur.

00:01:23.230 --> 00:01:29.780
The hammocks often have colorful names such as gooseneck, gator-roar, dead man.

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:39.460
and panther perch our story today deals with one of these islands and we call it a day at otter

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:50.020
hammock there is a peacefulness a timelessness a spaciousness to the everglades a feeling that

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:57.820
they go on forever the waters whether open or overgrown with luxuriant sawgrass are clear and

00:01:57.820 --> 00:01:59.800
fresh a great

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:05.710
But it is the hammocks which become the focal point for such life.

00:02:07.010 --> 00:02:08.410
Otter hammock is one of these.

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:15.290
Its dense growth of swamp trees help form an ideal habitat.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:19.520
Otter hammock has a small lake within it,

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:23.770
a lagoon-like body of water which attracts some of the larger animals,

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:25.880
like this big black bear.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:29.980
Here the animals find peace.

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:37.540
and solitude freedom from human interference a perfect place to live and they are active day and

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:45.370
night bobcats roam openly fearlessly in broad daylight even the deer are up and about this day

00:02:45.940 --> 00:02:54.240
quietly enjoying the cooler interior of otterham yet the prevailing peace does not mean that the

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:59.420
The wildlife which lives here has lost its wariness to the contrary.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:04.580
The raccoons retain their wariness as an ingrained characteristic.

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:12.570
They, and the armadillos, along with the other wild animal residents, must remain alert to survive.

00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:18.610
The otter is not only alert to danger, but is curious about any life nearby.

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:28.300
Terrapin, quietly sunning itself, does not escape the constant curiosity and mischievousness of the otter.

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:44.800
this log sloping into the water is one of the otter's favorite spots he's not

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:53.120
too pleased if someone else use it his curiosity about everything in his

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:58.660
territory above water or below makes him very familiar with the entire hammock

00:03:58.660 --> 00:03:59.940
habitat and the

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:16.140
other animals living here the sluggishness of this turtle does not long hold his interest

00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:25.070
and soon he leaves the reptile to itself for the otter who loves playing and exploring above all

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:29.780
the day holds many exciting things the grassy underwater

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:36.840
areas are warm and pleasant and he spends as much of his day here as he does on the hammock above

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:47.480
reveling in his enjoyment of both worlds. He is in this colorful below surface world in the realm of

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:53.430
the largemouth bass but today these fish don't hold his attention because of a sudden disturbance

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:59.980
nearby. The armadillo doesn't often intrude on the otter's domain like this since he

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:08.080
a clumsy swimmer at best because of his heavy armor he's far more at home on the hammock's dry ground

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:16.990
but sometimes he has to swim to reach a new area suddenly through the clear water the otter spies

00:05:16.990 --> 00:05:26.710
a bobcat walking on the shoreline above this is the otter's favorite log and the element of danger

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:29.770
involved in tempting a powerful and hungry bobcat.

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:37.130
is overshadowed by the fact that the otter is annoyed his territory has been infringed upon

00:05:37.130 --> 00:05:44.700
and he doesn't hesitate to let it be known at the same time he's very careful to stay

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:59.680
out of reach of the more powerful bobcat daughter there's a certain enjoyment and excitement

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:17.540
in skirting the danger by the very narrowest of margins the bobcat realizing the futility

00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:24.640
of this activity decides to look elsewhere in the hammock for prey the scent of an opossum

00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:29.970
on a low branch nearby is in the air and while opossum meat isn't the

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:39.640
number one choice. The bobcat is still curious enough to want a closer look. He's in no real

00:06:39.640 --> 00:06:46.060
hurry and knows that unless forced to flee, the opossum isn't going to leave his isolated tree

00:06:46.060 --> 00:06:59.970
which extends out over the water. Sluggish and dull and having poor defenses, the opossum

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:02.100
knows he's in danger right now.

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:21.170
The otter has been watching this little drama

00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:23.430
unfold in the branches over the water.

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:39.120
The otter moves in for a closer look only because he seldom gets a chance to see an opossum in the water.

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:44.550
The water is a safe retreat this time and has been an avenue of survival.

00:07:46.260 --> 00:07:49.460
On the other shore, the opossum will be safe from the bobcat.

00:08:01.340 --> 00:08:09.980
The very confinement of the hammocks makes confrontations between different wild animals occur frequently and often with unexpected results.

00:08:12.440 --> 00:08:17.140
The bobcat's hunger has not yet been appeased, and he's still actively hunting.

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:25.370
He's often dined on snakes in the past, and this big yellow rat snake could be next.

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:38.360
The rat snake's not venomous, so as part of its defense, it releases a pungent odor.

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:41.180
The effect of this is strange indeed.

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:46.140
As the snake coils tightly with no further attempt at defense,

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:50.030
the bobcat undergoes a sudden change of attitude.

00:08:50.950 --> 00:08:53.090
Its hunger is temporarily forgotten.

00:08:59.300 --> 00:08:59.960
The scent of the snake...

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:16.870
snake has affected the bobcat almost the same way that catnip affects a domestic cat seems to take

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:23.090
immense pleasure out of this rubbing forgetting practically everything else including hunger for

00:09:23.090 --> 00:09:23.430
a while

00:09:48.580 --> 00:09:56.050
Even when the pangs of hunger return abruptly to the bobcat, they are not directed against the snake, though it would make a good meal.

00:09:56.950 --> 00:09:59.630
Instead, the cat simply abandons the snake.

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:09.650
and resumes hunting with the bobcat well away in the hammock heading toward the water the yellow

00:10:09.650 --> 00:10:20.280
rat snake can resume its own activities none the worse for the encounter it's not long before the

00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:29.970
bobcat detects the scent of new prey this big mallard duck looks to be in perfect health but it's

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:38.000
not only a few days ago it struck a branch while landing and injured one of its wings now unable to

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:40.260
fly its life is in jeopardy

00:11:07.070 --> 00:11:11.080
Intuitively, the bobcat realizes something's wrong with this duck,

00:11:11.720 --> 00:11:13.400
and now the hunt is on in earnest.

00:11:41.960 --> 00:11:46.010
Nature's law has prevailed. Only the fittest survives.

00:11:52.660 --> 00:11:55.940
And now, as peace settles over the hammock again,

00:11:56.640 --> 00:11:59.920
the otter, himself becoming a little hungry, sets off.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.060
in a meandering way beneath the surface,

00:12:02.630 --> 00:12:06.050
ready to pursue any manner of prey which might cross his path.

00:12:41.100 --> 00:12:43.900
The otter's attention is attracted by a small splash,

00:12:44.320 --> 00:12:47.940
and he sees a leopard frog that has dived in from shore.

00:12:48.440 --> 00:12:50.080
Immediately, the chase is on.

00:13:00.890 --> 00:13:01.090
Thank you.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:53.850
There's no escape for this frog, despite its efforts to get away, but its death as food for the otter is also part of nature's plan, part of the cycle of life at Otter Hammock.

00:13:54.810 --> 00:13:59.970
This underwater activity has been detected by one of the most powerful predators of the Everglades.

00:14:00.510 --> 00:14:16.260
the alligator it is the only creature in the area which the otter very studiously avoids

00:14:16.260 --> 00:14:29.970
